1
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,250
I knew it!

2
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:23,540
It's coming!

3
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,370
The Female Titan!

4
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:33,700
After making a comeback,

5
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:38,040
the Female Titan took out the elite members
of the Levi Squad one after another.

6
00:00:43,950 --> 00:00:45,040
I'm going to kill her!

7
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:49,950
Blaming himself for trusting his comrades,
Eren made a resolute decision.

8
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:52,700
He fought in his transformed state...

9
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:00,450
...but the Female Titan
defeated him and took him away.

10
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:06,750
Give Eren...

11
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:08,660
...back!

12
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:21,450
Wherever you are,

13
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:25,700
I'm going to slaughter
this girl, butcher her body,

14
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:30,120
and get you out of that foul place...

15
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:32,330
Sorry, Eren...

16
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:36,790
Just hang on a little longer...

17
00:01:43,160 --> 00:01:44,580
Wait!

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,410
Wh-What...?!

19
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,870
Stay back for now.

20
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:30,500
<i>I won't let your deaths be meaningless</i>

21
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:36,620
<i>even if I'm the last one standing</i>

22
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,540
<i>In both hands, Gloria</i>

23
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,540
<i>What sings is Sieg</i>

24
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:52,750
<i>On my back, Flügel der Freiheit</i>

25
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:59,580
<i>Clenched determination to my left chest</i>

26
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:04,910
<i>What slashes across is Linie der Torheit</i>

27
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:08,160
<i>Soaring across the azure skies</i>

28
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:12,700
<i>Flügel der Freiheit</i>

29
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:31,290
"The Defeated"
"The 57th Exterior Scouting Mission, Part 6"

30
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:37,700
Maintain this distance.

31
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:42,290
She must be worn out, too.
She's not so fast anymore.

32
00:03:42,290 --> 00:03:45,200
It looked like she
bit the entire nape off.

33
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,830
Is Eren dead?

34
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:51,290
He's alive.

35
00:03:51,290 --> 00:03:53,620
The target seems intelligent

36
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:56,750
and intent on taking Eren away.

37
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:59,370
It'd crush him if it wanted to kill him.

38
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:05,540
Instead, it's fighting and running
away with him in its mouth.

39
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:08,290
Eating Eren could be her goal.

40
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:11,040
If so, he's in her stomach.

41
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:13,200
Which means he's probably dead.

42
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,620
He's alive.

43
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:18,790
Let's hope so.

44
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:23,120
This never would've
happened in the first place

45
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:25,750
had you actually protected Eren!

46
00:04:28,330 --> 00:04:32,040
Ah. You're that one who...

47
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:34,370
You're Eren's childhood friend.

48
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:39,000
Let's narrow our
goals down to one.

49
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,040
First, forget about taking her down.

50
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:45,830
She's killed so many of our comrades!

51
00:04:45,830 --> 00:04:49,290
It's impossible. She has
the ability to harden her skin.

52
00:04:49,290 --> 00:04:51,540
Do as I say.

53
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:54,950
We're going to set all
our hopes on Eren being alive

54
00:04:54,950 --> 00:04:57,660
and rescue him before
she leaves the forest.

55
00:04:57,660 --> 00:04:59,200
I'll do the cutting.

56
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:01,200
You distract her.

57
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:01,450
He's fast!

58
00:06:01,450 --> 00:06:04,660
She can't even
harden her skin in time!

59
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:18,790
Her nape...

60
00:06:18,790 --> 00:06:20,200
It's wide open!

61
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:23,450
She's worn-down!
I doubt she can move now!

62
00:06:23,450 --> 00:06:25,080
I can kill her!

63
00:06:27,910 --> 00:06:29,330
Stop!

64
00:06:43,750 --> 00:06:45,160
Eren!

65
00:06:51,830 --> 00:06:53,290
Hey!

66
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:55,500
Time to go!

67
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,910
Eren!

68
00:06:58,410 --> 00:07:02,500
He seems fine.
He's filthy, but alive.

69
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:06,370
Forget about her now.
We need to withdraw.

70
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:10,160
Don't lose sight of
what this operation is about.

71
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:13,950
Is wallowing in self-indulgence
more important?

72
00:07:13,950 --> 00:07:16,450
He's a dear friend to you, isn't he?

73
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:22,120
No... I'm...

74
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:41,830
They're coming back already?

75
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:43,950
What happened?

76
00:07:43,950 --> 00:07:45,790
Dunno.

77
00:07:45,790 --> 00:07:49,660
But I bet they'll be bringing back
another load of corpses with 'em.

78
00:08:05,250 --> 00:08:08,290
It sounds like Eld is on his way back.

79
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,410
Oh...

80
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:19,790
Think ol' Oruo will have
time to stop by home?

81
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:23,330
I'll set a plate for him just in case!

82
00:08:27,450 --> 00:08:30,200
Gunther is coming back, you know.

83
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:35,200
I see...

84
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:39,700
This is the one thing
I'll never get used to...

85
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:42,830
I doubt <i>anyone </i>could.

86
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:46,160
How my comrades are gonna die...

87
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:49,000
How <i>I'm </i>gonna die...

88
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,580
That's all I start to think about...

89
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:56,160
I try not to think about it at all.

90
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:59,160
Because if I started
picturing my own death,

91
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:02,700
I'd probably lose the ability to fight...

92
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:05,120
Yeah.

93
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:08,290
You're exactly right.

94
00:10:12,950 --> 00:10:16,250
How long do you
think we can survive?

95
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:20,000
We've managed
to survive so far, at least.

96
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,040
Yeah, so far.

97
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:26,910
We should be glad. We're still alive.

98
00:10:26,910 --> 00:10:30,660
Can you say that to the
bodies of the guys who died?

99
00:10:37,620 --> 00:10:41,750
We might never get to
see our hometowns again.

100
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:46,580
We're nearly finished, Sir.

101
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:50,200
Five bodies or so
were unrecoverable, however.

102
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:52,120
Not even pieces of them?

103
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:55,450
The Titans didn't
leave much to recover.

104
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:01,700
I feel it'd be better for the families
if we <i>didn't </i>bring back what's left.

105
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,500
Put them down as "missing."

106
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:04,910
Yes, Sir.

107
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:09,500
We've spotted several
Titans in the vicinity of the forest,

108
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,500
but none are yet headed this way.

109
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,750
We move at once. Inform the squads.

110
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:16,750
Yes, Sir!

111
00:11:16,750 --> 00:11:19,410
I refuse to accept this, Commander Erwin!

112
00:11:19,410 --> 00:11:21,500
H-Hey, you!

113
00:11:21,500 --> 00:11:23,080
We <i>should </i>recover them!

114
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:26,200
Ivan's body was
right there in front of us!

115
00:11:26,200 --> 00:11:28,620
There were Titans there too!

116
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:30,790
We could end up
as casualties ourselves!

117
00:11:30,790 --> 00:11:34,330
Then we can just
take 'em out if they attack!

118
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:37,040
Ivan and I grew up in the same town!

119
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,910
I know his parents, too!

120
00:11:38,910 --> 00:11:41,160
I'd at least like to take him home!

121
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,450
Quit being selfish!

122
00:11:42,450 --> 00:11:44,950
A bunch of brats arguing...

123
00:11:44,950 --> 00:11:46,830
Captain Levi!

124
00:11:46,830 --> 00:11:50,500
If you've confirmed his death,
then that's enough.

125
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:56,500
He's dead. Whether or not we
have his body makes no difference.

126
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:58,450
You can't be serious...

127
00:11:58,450 --> 00:12:01,250
Ivan and the others
will be put down as "missing."

128
00:12:01,250 --> 00:12:04,700
That decision is final. Just let it go.

129
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:08,790
D-Do neither of you...

130
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:12,250
...have any human feelings at all?!

131
00:12:12,250 --> 00:12:15,700
Hey, Dieter! Watch what you're saying!

132
00:12:59,870 --> 00:13:01,290
Titans!

133
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,200
That's...

134
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:13,000
...Dieter!

135
00:13:16,790 --> 00:13:18,620
That idiot!

136
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:24,410
Titan spotted by the rear!

137
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:26,040
Full speed!

138
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:29,830
I don't see any large trees <i>or </i>buildings.

139
00:13:29,830 --> 00:13:32,200
We can't fight freely out here.

140
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:35,200
Fleeing to the wall will be quicker.

141
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:02,950
It's about to catch up to us!

142
00:14:02,950 --> 00:14:05,410
We're gonna have to fight!

143
00:14:05,410 --> 00:14:08,330
ODM can't accomplish much on flat ground.

144
00:14:08,330 --> 00:14:10,160
Plus, look.

145
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,790
They just keep coming!

146
00:14:12,330 --> 00:14:15,540
Then what do <i>you </i>suggest we do?!

147
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,160
We need to...

148
00:14:54,790 --> 00:14:56,660
It's no use! It's catching up!

149
00:14:56,660 --> 00:14:58,250
I'll get behind it and distract it!

150
00:14:58,250 --> 00:15:01,580
--Use that chance--
--Don't bother.

151
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:05,120
Dump the bodies. Before it catches up.

152
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,910
B-But, Sir...!

153
00:15:06,910 --> 00:15:10,910
There've been countless people
before whose bodies were left behind.

154
00:15:10,910 --> 00:15:13,540
These ones aren't somehow special.

155
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:16,500
Are we going to do it?!

156
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,870
Are we really going to do it?!

157
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:23,950
Damn...

158
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:28,620
We got no other choice!

159
00:15:57,370 --> 00:15:59,040
That's it!

160
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:00,870
Keep moving!

161
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:15,540
We leave as soon as
we've confirmed our positions!

162
00:16:15,540 --> 00:16:17,410
Stay sharp!

163
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:21,160
We need to make a slight
course correction to the east.

164
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:31,080
Captain Levi...

165
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:32,500
I...

166
00:16:35,830 --> 00:16:39,580
This is proof that they once lived.

167
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:42,040
That's how I see it, anyway.

168
00:16:45,790 --> 00:16:47,620
It's Ivan's.

169
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,500
Captain...

170
00:17:11,450 --> 00:17:13,080
Let's move out!

171
00:17:32,330 --> 00:17:36,620
Eren. I'd forget about the
Scout Regiment if I were you.

172
00:17:36,620 --> 00:17:40,120
What?! You think the
Scout Regiment is a joke too?!

173
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:43,200
It's not about what I think.

174
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:51,950
The Scout Regiment is back!

175
00:17:51,950 --> 00:17:53,830
They're gonna open the front gate!

176
00:17:53,830 --> 00:17:56,580
Let's go see the heroes return, Mikasa!

177
00:17:56,580 --> 00:17:58,000
Oh...!

178
00:18:15,830 --> 00:18:18,910
They're the only ones who made it back?

179
00:18:18,910 --> 00:18:21,700
Everyone else must've gotten eaten.

180
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:25,160
This is what they get
for going outside the walls.

181
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:30,160
Our taxes are basically going to feeding
and fattening those things up now.

182
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,580
Eren.

183
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,500
What's wrong?

184
00:18:45,910 --> 00:18:47,330
Eren...

185
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:54,080
Eren!

186
00:19:02,790 --> 00:19:04,200
Eren?

187
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,160
You shouldn't get up yet.

188
00:19:12,910 --> 00:19:14,540
You need to rest.

189
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:18,080
Where's the Female Titan?!

190
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,120
She got away.

191
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:21,700
Why?

192
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:25,250
Why did everyone...?

193
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:27,500
What about the operation?

194
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,580
It failed.

195
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:31,950
You need to rest for now.

196
00:19:33,700 --> 00:19:35,620
How did I get this?

197
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:39,870
Did you save me again?

198
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:46,330
We're almost to the wall now.

199
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:07,120
Is it me, or are there
fewer than this morning?

200
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:10,080
A <i>lot </i>fewer.

201
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,330
Another bad one...

202
00:20:13,290 --> 00:20:17,580
They left this morning shouting and
roaring, and now they're already back?

203
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:19,750
What did they even leave for?

204
00:20:19,750 --> 00:20:21,700
Beats me.

205
00:20:21,700 --> 00:20:26,200
But from the brooding
looks on their faces...

206
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:30,500
...I'd say they succeeded in
pouring our tax money down the drain.

207
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,700
Eren. Endure it.

208
00:20:46,290 --> 00:20:47,830
So cool!

209
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:50,330
The Scout Regiment's awesome!

210
00:20:50,330 --> 00:20:54,250
Even when they're so
beat-up they keep on fighting!

211
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,080
Captain Levi, Sir!

212
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:18,290
Thanks for looking after my daughter!

213
00:21:18,290 --> 00:21:19,910
I'm Petra's father!

214
00:21:19,910 --> 00:21:23,660
I'd like to discuss something
before she spots me...

215
00:21:23,660 --> 00:21:26,580
She sent me a letter, you see...

216
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:30,540
She said she was assigned to serve
you because you recognized her skill.

217
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:33,410
She said she wants to devote her all to you...

218
00:21:33,410 --> 00:21:35,410
Basically, the girl's so starry-eyed

219
00:21:35,410 --> 00:21:39,160
that she has no idea how worried her parents are!

220
00:21:39,950 --> 00:21:44,040
So, well, as her father, you see...

221
00:21:44,040 --> 00:21:47,330
I feel it's a bit too early
to let her get married.

222
00:21:47,330 --> 00:21:51,540
She's still young and
has so much to experience...

223
00:21:51,540 --> 00:21:52,790
Commander Erwin!

224
00:21:52,790 --> 00:21:54,540
Please answer us!

225
00:21:54,540 --> 00:21:58,370
Were the gains from this expedition
worth the number of lives lost?!

226
00:21:58,370 --> 00:22:02,160
Do you honestly believe the
soldiers died without regrets?!

227
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:10,120
The costs and casualties incurred
by this latest exterior expedition

228
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:15,160
dealt a blow heavy enough to
destroy the Scout Regiment's support.

229
00:22:24,290 --> 00:22:29,870
Erwin and the others in charge found
themselves summoned to the capital

230
00:22:30,450 --> 00:22:33,660
and ordered to hand over Eren.

231
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:57,750
<i>If, by chance, I'm not me</i>

232
00:22:57,750 --> 00:23:03,000
<i>then who's to say that you're you?</i>

233
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:08,290
<i>Can you pick up the pieces of your heart</i>

234
00:23:08,290 --> 00:23:13,410
<i>that fell apart like a broken sand castle?</i>

235
00:23:13,410 --> 00:23:18,410
<i>The voice of someone calling out</i>

236
00:23:18,410 --> 00:23:22,500
<i>changed into ringing in my ears</i>

237
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:27,660
<i>It's as if time has stopped</i>

238
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:30,450
<i>Now wake up</i>

239
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:35,750
<i>I made my way out of the deep darkness</i>

240
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:41,000
<i>I fled like a swift wind</i>

241
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:48,500
<i>We used to be like living corpses,</i>

242
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:50,540
<i>but now we head beyond the walls</i>

243
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:52,580
<i>Let's meet again</i>

244
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:57,410
<i>in a place not on any map</i>

245
00:24:09,540 --> 00:24:12,410
Annie is assigned to
the security escort team

246
00:24:12,410 --> 00:24:15,450
the day Eren and the others
are summoned to the royal capital.

247
00:24:15,450 --> 00:24:18,540
From out of nowhere, Armin appears

248
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:21,410
and asks for her help
in a top-secret operation.

249
00:24:21,410 --> 00:24:23,370
"Smile"
"Assault on Stohess, Part 1"
